     1,
     "Dear Phil and everybody in this group,<div><br></div><div>Thanks for accepting my joining request.</div><div>I have outcomes of the simdata() function I cannot explain despite studying the references for the  mirt package. I would be very thankful for your help.</div><div>I am conducting a simulation study on H coefficients and use mirt for simulating the data sets. I noted that the exact population H coefficients I calculate (via integration) based on a and b parameters are constantly different (+.03-.05) from the estimated H coefficients (mokken::coefH()) based on data from <span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mirt</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\">::simdata(</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">a</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\"> = rep(</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1.5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\">), </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">d</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\"> = seq(</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">-1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">length.out</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\"> = </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\">), </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">N</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\"> = </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1000000</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">itemtype</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\"> = </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px;color:rgb(158,0,3)\">&quot;2PL&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\">). </span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\"><br></span></div><div><font color=\"#060087\" face=\"Monaco\"><span style=\"font-size:12.199999809265137px\">I tried to understand how simdata() works and used base R for simulating: </span></font></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(62,62,62);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12.2px\"># set parameters</span></div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">a</span> = rep(<span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1.5</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">5</span>)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b</span> = seq(<span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">-1</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">length.out</span> = <span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">5</span>)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(11,66,19)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135)\"> = </span>1000000</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ni</span> = length(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">a</span>)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(62,62,62)\"># simulating population with base R</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">pl2</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(181,118,12)\">function</span> (<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">theta</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">a</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b</span>) {</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p</span> &lt;- exp(<span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1.0</span>*<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">a</span>*(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">theta</span>-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b</span>)) / (<span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1</span>+exp(<span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1.0</span>*<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">a</span>*(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">theta</span>-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b</span>)))</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  return(</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">    <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  )<span style=\"font-size:12.2px\">}</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(62,62,62)\"># take a random sample of size n, create data frame</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">theta</span> &lt;- rnorm(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">n</span>)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data</span> &lt;- data.frame(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">theta</span>)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(62,62,62)\"># calculate probabilities based on theta, a, b.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(181,118,12)\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i2</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(181,118,12)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ni</span>) {</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(62,62,62)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  </span># define item difficulty and open item vector</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">bi</span> = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i2</span>]</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ai</span> = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">a</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i2</span>]</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">item</span> = c()</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(62,62,62)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  </span># apply pl2 function over every theta</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  <span style=\"color:rgb(181,118,12)\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(181,118,12)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">n</span>) {</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">    <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p</span> &lt;- pl2(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">theta</span> = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">theta</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span>],<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">a</span> = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ai</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b</span> = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">bi</span>)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">      <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">item</span>[<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">i</span>] &lt;- rbinom(<span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(11,66,19)\">1</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">p</span>)       </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">    }</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(62,62,62)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  </span># attach item to data</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data</span> &lt;- cbind(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data</span>,<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">item</span>)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">}</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">The H coefficients I estimate from my base R simulation match the exact population H I calculated. So my questions is, how is that possible and where exactly does the simdata() function different steps than I do using base R.</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">Thanks in advance! </p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">I attach an example script if necessary.</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">All the best</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 4px;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12.2px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(6,0,135)\">Sebastian</p>"
    ]
   ]
